meta {
  name: Collection Summary Grouped
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/orders/collection-summary/grouped?statuses=ORDER,APPOINTMENT,CANCELLED&groupBy=b2b
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  statuses: ORDER,APPOINTMENT,CANCELLED
  groupBy: b2b
  ~dateFrom: 2026-07-01
  ~dateTo: 2026-07-31
  ~branchId: {{branchId}}
  ~paymentMode: UPI
  ~search: john
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Grouped Collection aggregate powering the dimension panels — the realization view
  of `/orders/billing-summary/grouped` (same shared grouping layer with
  `report:'collection'`). `groupBy` = `b2b` | `ref-by` | `internal-referral` |
  `external-referral` | `int-ref-user` | `ext-ref-user` | `outsource` (order-level) or
  `lab-test` | `lab-panel` | `department` | `category` | `subcategory` (item-level,
  allocated). Grouping matches the Billing endpoint:

  - `lab-test` / `lab-panel` group by the stable test/panel **code** (same test
    across pricing lists → one row); panels group only panel lines.
  - `department` / `category` / `subcategory` resolve the classification as **branch
    scalar ?? master catalogue** (via `sourceLabTestId` / `sourceLabPanelId`); both
    tests and panels contribute, no individual test/panel rows.
  - `internal-referral` / `external-referral` are re-sourced to accession
    `SampleTransfer`s: internal groups by the **destination branch**, external by the
    **external partner**; money is order-level.
  - `int-ref-user` / `ext-ref-user` group by the internal / external referral **user**
    from the order's Referral Details (`internalReferralId` / `externalReferralId`).
  - `outsource` groups by the **outsource center** of the order's accession
    `SampleTransfer` (`kind=OUTSOURCE`).

  Each row returns the totals + the five-mode payment breakdown (`cash` / `upi` /
  `bankTransfer` / `debitCard` / `creditCard`, WALLET excluded), where
  `Σ modes === paid`. `Σ groups` reconciles with `/orders/collection-summary` and
  `/orders/collection-records` for the same dimension + filters.
}
